# A Structure of the caller's data binds dynamically before the lexical levels, as a number does (plan M11 5b; R20,
# item 4): inner, written in the code of main, reads the Point of outer's data, not the Point of main.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the
# call main().
sub: main () (
    Point: a b
    int: seen 0
)
    fn: inner () int
        return: length(Point)
    fn: outer () int (
        Point: a b c
    )
        return: inner()
    seen := outer()
main()
int: seen main\data\seen
